    "chunk_text": "1AIV (w) jeks fldgi \u2014 Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'05'29PART IV(A) \u2014 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 29.05.2019\n\nw;s \u00fafYI\n\nwxl 2125$45 - 2019 uehs ui 29 jeks nodod - 2019'05'29No. 2125/45 - WEDNESDAY MAY 29, 2019\n\nEXTRAORDINARYThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\n(Published by Authority)PART IV (A) \u2014 PROVINCIAL COUNCILS\n\nY%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\nProvincial Councils Notifications\n\n1A - PG 4534 \u2014 89 (05/2019)\n\nWESTERN PROVINCE PROVINCIAL COUNCIL\n\nNotification made under Section 2(2) of Entertainment Tax Ordinance No. 12 of 1946\n\nI, Isura Devapriya, the Chief Minister of Western Province and the Minister of Finance and Planning, Engineering Services,Law and Order, Local Government and Provincial Administration, Economic Promotions, Power and Energy, EnvironmentalAffairs, Water Supply and Drainage and Tourism of Western Province do hereby notify that permission is granted underand by virtue of powers vested in me by provision of Section 2(2) of the Entertainment Tax Ordinance No. 12 of 1946 thathas to be read with Section 2 of Provincial Councils (Consequential Provisions) Act, No. 12 of 1989, to impose andrecover the entertainment tax of 15% out of the entrance fee that is recovered for the entertainment activities as per termsof expression in Entertainment Tax Ordinance No. 12 of 1946, that is amended by (Amendment) of Entertainment TaxAct, No. 37 of 1984, however as per provisions of Section 2(1) of Entertainment Tax Ordinance No. 12 of 1946, theresolution that has been passed in the meeting held on 19.07.2018 in the Pradeshiya Sabha of Homagama, to impose andrecover 10% of the entertainment tax, for the displays those are displayed in the cinema halls, which fall within theadministrative limit of Homagama Pradeshiya Sabhawa."
